=== writer's 22 tests on mut-nobump-areaenter
PASS	arming, eligible target, requests and duplicate guard
PASS	conversation invalid and distant or party exclusions
PASS	transient inner PC failure allows retry
PASS	party min-one-HP guard restores each prior flag after settle, transition and unload
PASS	unreadable prior min-one-HP flag leaves that party member untouched
PASS	module load re-resolves a guarded party member whose object ID changed
PASS	module load re-resolves the guarded PC through GetFirstPC when its object ID changed
PASS	module load restores the original PC while it is still valid; a new GetFirstPC object is left alone
PASS	a PC swap onto another guarded member restores both objects to their own priors
PASS	a gone PC is never resolved onto another member this script guarded under its own ID
PASS	a member that cannot be re-resolved is recorded and retried; every resolvable guard is still cleared
PASS	R3-1: two PC entries recreated after a load each go back to their own creature
PASS	R3-2: a PC recreated under an ID the script used before a load is restored, and its stuck flag never becomes a prior
PASS	R3-3: a companion recreated under a recycled ID after a load is restored by tag
PASS	R3-5: after a load, a valid stored ID with the same tag that is not a party member is not the companion
PASS	a non-party creature with the companion tag is never taken for the companion; the entry stays pending
PASS	R3-4: unload restores everyone it can find and names each creature it cannot, with the console fix
PASS	an old ID recycled onto another untagged party member after a load is not trusted; the PC is found through GetFirstPC
PASS	two entries that resolve to one creature after a load give an unknown prior, restored to 0 and logged
PASS	an untagged member that cannot be found after a load keeps its first prior when a blast reaches it again
PASS	frag VFX is unreachable when blast deaths arrive after the hook returns
PASS	frag VFX is reached only if a death script re-enters during the damage call
